  "verbalization": "Sansalvamide A is implicated in the biological activity of SNU-387 through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in the same pathway of molecular interaction. The evidence suggests that Sansalvamide A acts as a target for multiple compounds, including MIP, which in turn is the target of other molecules such as 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol. These compounds all ultimately target SNU-387, indicating a shared mechanism of action or a common pathway of molecular interaction. The presence of multiple targets for Sansalvamide A suggests that it may interact with various molecular entities that ultimately lead to the activation or modulation of SNU-387. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Sansalvamide A and SNU-387, emphasizing the importance of understanding the molecular mechanisms underlying their interaction.",
